	"system": {
		"description": "<p>You create an invisible forcefield at a point you choose. The forcefield is 1/4 inch thick and can be free floating or resting or connected to a solid surface. You may form it into a hemispherical dome or sphere, either with a radius of up to 10 feet. Alternatively, you may create a horizontal, vertical, or diagonal surface made up of up to a contiguous group of ten 10-foot square sections. If the force field enters a creature’s space when it appears, the creature is pushed to one side of the wall (your choice), but when a creature would be surrounded on all sides by the force field (or the force field and another solid surface) it can use its reaction to make a Dexterity saving throw to move up to its Speed to escape. Any creature without a special sense like blindsight has disadvantage on this saving throw. Nothing can physically pass through the force field. It can be destroyed with a successful use of surged psionic disruption or by being dealt at least 10 force damage by a single attack or effect. It is otherwise immune to damage.</p><p><strong>Surge.</strong> You can spend +1 psionic point to increase the duration to Concentration (10 minutes) [requires power rating IV].5: Psionics</p>",
